course: dictionary
lesson: 4360
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. Gun is a good example. «Aim water guns at the body, not the face, and only at people who are playing too.» Here a gun is a toy that squirts water, because the sentence is about playing.
explain: «Let an adult help with a hot glue gun.» The adult helping tells you this gun is a tool, not a toy or a weapon. The clues are the words around the word. Always ask: what does this word have to mean for the sentence to make sense? Then swap your meaning in and check.
explain: Safety comes first. A real gun is never a toy, and you must never assume it is unloaded. If you ever find a real gun, STOP, DON'T TOUCH, LEAVE the area and TELL a grown-up straight away.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A gun is a weapon that fires bullets or other objects through a metal tube using explosive force.
fact: A gun can also be a tool that shoots something out, like a water gun, glue gun or starting gun.
fact: A starting gun begins a race.
fact: «Jump the gun» means to start too soon, and «stick to your guns» means not to change your mind.
exercise: «Aim water guns at the body, not the face.» What is a water gun in this sentence? | A school bell | A weapon that fires bullets | *A toy that squirts water | A kind of cake
exercise: «Let an adult help with a hot glue gun.» What is a glue gun? | A weapon for a sports game | A tall tower in a park | *A tool that shoots out hot glue | A special kind of paint
exercise: «The starting gun went off, and the runners began.» What does a starting gun do? | *It begins the race | It counts the laps | It stops the race | It gives out prizes
test: «He wanted to jump the gun and start before the whistle.» What does jump the gun mean? | *Start too soon | Shout very loudly | Stop and wait | Jump over a fence
test: You find a real gun in a park. What should you do first? | Pick it up to look closely | *Stop, don't touch it, leave the area and tell a grown-up | Fire it to see if it works | Take it home to show your friends
exam: Which statement about a real gun is always true? | It cannot hurt anyone | It is always safe to touch | *Never assume it is a toy or unloaded | It is always a toy
